VTID-03819 — commands.log
==========================

## Research (background agent) before writing any code

Traced the actual task-creation call chain rather than assuming one:
- services/gateway/src/services/gemini-operator.ts:991 (executeCreateTask,
  the autopilot_create_task tool handler) and
  services/gateway/src/routes/operator.ts:228 (slash-command intake) both
  funnel through ONE choke point:
  services/gateway/src/services/operator-service.ts:967 createOperatorTask().
- Confirmed existing embedding infra to reuse (VTID-01184):
  services/gateway/src/services/embedding-service.ts's generateEmbedding()
  (1536-dim, OpenAI-primary/Gemini-fallback) and the pgvector pattern in
  services/gateway/src/services/supabase-semantic-memory.ts's
  memory_semantic_search RPC (supabase.rpc() with embedding formatted as a
  '[v1,v2,...]' string).
- Confirmed vtid_ledger has NO embedding column (DATABASE_SCHEMA.md) — a new
  additive column + RPC is needed, modeled directly on the existing
  memory_items HNSW-index pattern
  (supabase/migrations/20260117140000_vtid_01184_pgvector_semantic_memory.sql).
- Confirmed no existing "duplicate task"/"related task" feature anywhere in
  the repo (grepped "duplicate", "similar_task", "related_task", "dedup") —
  the closest precedent is intent-find-match.ts's search-before-create
  pattern for a different domain (Discover intent catalog), reused here as
  the design template, not copy-pasted.

## Schema change

$ mcp__Supabase__apply_migration name=vtid_03819_ledger_dedup_embedding
  ALTER TABLE vtid_ledger ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS embedding vector(1536) NULL;
  ALTER TABLE vtid_ledger ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS embedding_updated_at timestamptz NULL;
  CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_vtid_ledger_embedding_hnsw ON vtid_ledger
    USING hnsw (embedding vector_cosine_ops) WITH (m = 16, ef_construction = 64);
  CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION find_similar_vtid_tasks(...) ...
-> {"success": true}

See outputs/live-verification.txt for the full schema/index/RPC verification
transcript, including a live smoke-test call to the RPC.

## Code changes

- New services/gateway/src/services/ledger-task-dedup.ts:
  checkForSimilarTask(title, description) — embeds the text via the existing
  generateEmbedding(), calls find_similar_vtid_tasks via REST RPC, and
  classifies the closest match as `duplicate` (>=0.93 similarity) or
  `related` (0.80-0.93). Fails OPEN (returns {}) on any missing config,
  embedding failure, or RPC error — dedup is an availability enhancement,
  never a precondition for task creation.
  stampTaskEmbedding(vtid, title, description) — fire-and-forget PATCH of
  the embedding column on a just-created row, so future checks can find it.
- operator-service.ts's createOperatorTask(): calls checkForSimilarTask()
  BEFORE allocateVtid() (no point minting a VTID for a request that's the
  same as an existing task). A `duplicate` match short-circuits — returns
  the EXISTING vtid/title with `duplicate: true`, no allocation, no ledger
  write, no spec event. A `related` match still creates the task normally
  but stamps `metadata.related_vtid`/`related_similarity`. On any successful
  creation, stampTaskEmbedding() is fired (not awaited for the return value)
  so the new row's own embedding gets populated.
- gemini-operator.ts's executeCreateTask(): when createdTask.duplicate is
  true, skips the vtid.created OASIS event + "executed" intent log (nothing
  was actually created) and returns a message naming the existing VTID.
- routes/operator.ts: distinguishes the duplicate case in its console log
  only (same createOperatorTask() call, so the dedup logic applies here too
  with no extra wiring needed).
- Command Hub frontend (app.js/styles.css): new createRelatedTaskChip(task)
  reads task.metadata.related_vtid, renders a "Related: VTID-XXXXX" pill
  (new .task-related-chip CSS class, modeled on the existing
  .task-card-status-pill pattern) on both the task card and the drawer
  header; clicking it reuses the EXISTING state.taskSearchQuery board filter
  (no new navigation built).
- scripts/ci/command-hub-ownership-guard.js: registered VTID-03819 in the
  Command Hub Path Ownership Guard allowlist (same per-VTID pattern as
  VTID-03818), since this VTID touches the protected command-hub tree.

